                <pb facs="0792" n="696" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg696"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 6 in No. 108.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Messrs. McDonald &amp;
                            Dare to the managers of the Oriental Bank
                            Corporation.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Yokohama</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-08-05"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 5,
                        1874</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The least rate obtainable for any large
                    amount of bank-bills at sight would not, we consider, be better than 4s. 1¼,
                    (four shillings and a penny farthing.)</p>
                <p>We are, sir, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>M<hi rendition="#small-caps">c</hi>DONALD &amp; DARE,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bill and Bullion Brokers.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
